    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17ba346c_55a175e1",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 465,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-08T21:19:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "would be nicer to not have this command at all, and instead enable SPI mode when and only when we want to assert chip select.  Reduces the chances of being in an unexpected mode.\nThis would also minimize the time spent in SPI mode, so that reset, power button, and the uarts will work as expected when sequencing an AP flash write without injecting this command.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 465,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 465,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ca23fca155348c3810d3841c3f4b1dbe50f44b73",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ea61d91_4754690c",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 465,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-08T23:11:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Talked offline, and I agree that this is a cool feature that we can probably do soon.\n\nOut flash_ap script will take care of the on and off business now, and we can easily change that when we implement the auto detection feature. I would want that to be a follow up CL. I will file a bug for it",
      "parentUuid": "17ba346c_55a175e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 465,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 465,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ca23fca155348c3810d3841c3f4b1dbe50f44b73",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e509d19a_caa7a56e",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 479,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-08T21:08:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we shouldn\u0027t have to specify the SPI Vref.\nWhen the mux is swung to SPI mode, the H1 VREF signal becomes the SPI VREF voltage (and technically the EC VREF signal is also the SPI VREF voltage).  So we should detect it.\n\nEven more importantly, if we swing the mux and do not see a voltage on SPI_VREF/H1_VREF, that means the flash chip is unpowered and we should probably return an error code.  The user should have used the Cr50 UART to assert AP_FLASH_ENABLE to force power onto the SPI flash before switching into SPI mode.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 479,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "ca23fca155348c3810d3841c3f4b1dbe50f44b73",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0605bff_48c4adec",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 479,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-08T23:11:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per our conversation, the initial version will handle the manually setting Vref for the SPI lines. I am filing bugs for this request.",
      "parentUuid": "e509d19a_caa7a56e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 479,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "ca23fca155348c3810d3841c3f4b1dbe50f44b73",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
